// 2756
[struct_2756]
param=param_2095,Nomad
param=param_2096,1
param=param_2153,npc_14497
param=param_2168,npc_14498
param=param_2123,37
param=param_2124,31
param=param_2097,4
param=param_2184,Nomad is an incredibly proud warrior. He doesn't think twice at killing others or even harvesting the souls of innocents. Probably best to not mention that he's somewhat bald.<br><br><col=F5B241>Quest</col>: Nomad's Requiem<br><br><col=F5B241>Combat</col>: As the final boss in a high-level quest he offers a horrific battle involving duplicates of himself, proximity mines, and a devastating attack from which you'd better try to hide. Plus, he replenishes his own health. He also has an attack where he teleports you into the centre of the arena, freezes you and proceeds to take away all your life points except 1.
param=param_2102,Prepare to meet death
param=param_2118,vorbis_7977
param=param_2119,vorbis_7977
param=param_2120,vorbis_7977
param=param_2121,vorbis_7977
param=param_2122,10000
param=param_2099,0
param=param_2101,aif_dom_nomad

// 2757
[struct_2757]
param=param_2095,Pest Queen (+ Drones)
param=param_2096,2
param=param_2153,npc_14444
param=param_2168,npc_14445
param=param_2123,28
param=param_2124,30
param=param_2097,2
param=param_2184,This giant monster is a mother to the pests that plague the void knights. Big, squirmy, and covered in eyes and tentacles; it's best not to get too close!<br><br><col=F5B241>Quest</col>: The Void Stares Back<br><br><col=F5B241>Combat</col>: She spawns drones that, in turn, spawn defilers. You must keep the queen's helpers at bay so your fellow knights can stop the queen from healing herself. You need to use the special attack on Korasi's sword (provided in the arena) to stop the queen from obliterating the knights.
param=param_2102,Gnraar
param=param_2118,vorbis_8630
param=param_2119,vorbis_8630
param=param_2120,vorbis_8630
param=param_2121,vorbis_8630
param=param_2122,20000
param=param_2099,2
param=param_2101,aif_dom_pest_queen_drone

// 2758
[struct_2758]
param=param_2095,Decaying Avatar
param=param_2096,3
param=param_2153,npc_14493
param=param_2168,npc_14494
param=param_2123,35
param=param_2124,29
param=param_2097,1
param=param_2184,Probably the tallest monster ever to exist, this lumbering beast embodies destruction and decay.<br><br><col=F5B241>Quest</col>: Nomad's Requiem<br><br><col=F5B241>Combat</col>: A fearsome foe that replenishes his health from the roots that appear around the arena. Remove the roots to avoid the avatar replenishing itself and the fight taking longer than it needs to.
param=param_2102,Grrr
param=param_2118,vorbis_8252
param=param_2119,vorbis_8252
param=param_2120,vorbis_8252
param=param_2121,vorbis_8252
param=param_2122,10000
param=param_2099,1
param=param_2101,aif_dom_decaying_avatar

// 2759
[struct_2759]
param=param_2095,Eruni, Ayuni and Leeuni
param=param_2096,4
param=param_2153,npc_14600
param=param_2154,npc_14601
param=param_2155,npc_14602
param=param_2168,npc_14603
param=param_2169,npc_14605
param=param_2170,npc_14606
param=param_2123,35
param=param_2124,32
param=param_2125,35
param=param_2126,29
param=param_2127,38
param=param_2128,30
param=param_2097,4
param=param_2184,These beasts were created by Amascut who stole the hearing, sound and sight of Apmeken in order to create the deadly trio. There's something incredibly creepy about a foe who hides their face behind a mask...<br><br><col=F5B241>Quest</col>: Do no Evil<br><br><col=F5B241>Combat</col>: Fight these three together you'll have several things to worry about. Ayuni will teleport towards you if you get too far away; attacks with melee and magic and will drain your prayer. Leeuni attacks with melee and magic and will teleport to get up close and personal should you stray too far away. Leeuni will also remove the various versions of the slayer facemasks and helmets should you choose to wear one. Eruni attacks with magic and is invincible while there are any demons around (oh yes, by the way you have to fight demons at the same time).
param=param_2102,Do you hear that? Sounds like defeat
param=param_2103,Iiii see you
param=param_2104,Delicious, tasty mortal
param=param_2118,vorbis_8049
param=param_2119,vorbis_8049
param=param_2120,vorbis_8049
param=param_2121,vorbis_8049
param=param_2122,11000
param=param_2099,0
param=param_2101,aif_dom_ay_er_le

// 2760
[struct_2760]
param=param_2095,Zenevivia
param=param_2096,5
param=param_2153,npc_14572
param=param_2168,npc_14573
param=param_2123,38
param=param_2124,32
param=param_2097,5
param=param_2184,A sweetheart of the Wise Old Man. With her love of combat she is ready to show just how mean she can be!<br><br><col=F5B241>Quest</col>: Love Story<br><br><col=F5B241>Combat</col>: During her onslaught, she teleports around to pedestals, and you should knock her off these in order to damage her. Watch out for her spawning fire. At least the Wise Old Man is there to help!
param=param_2102,Be prepared to meet your maker!
param=param_2118,vorbis_8077
param=param_2119,vorbis_8077
param=param_2120,vorbis_8077
param=param_2121,vorbis_8077
param=param_2122,3500
param=param_2099,0
param=param_2101,aif_dom_zenevivia

// 2761
[struct_2761]
param=param_2095,Dagannoth Mother (Version 2)
param=param_2096,6
param=param_2153,npc_14504
param=param_2168,npc_14505
param=param_2123,36
param=param_2124,30
param=param_2097,3
param=param_2184,One of the most dangerous types of dagannoth, she is the daughter of the first dagannoth to terrorise the Fremennik. Through many generations they have developed a unique set of defensive and offensive abilities. Beware!<br><br><col=F5B241>Quest</col>: Blood Runs Deep<br><br><col=F5B241>Combat</col>: To start with, you'll need to hit her with Balmung (weapon provided in arena), then she will switch at random between different combat types, requiring you to use different attack styles to deal damage to her. Be prepared to use melee, ranged and magic attacks unless you fancy a very long battle. She will attack with magic, melee and ranged attacks. You'll need to remember: blue (water magic); orange (melee attacks); green (ranged attacks); brown (earth magic); red (fire magic); white (air magic).<br><br>If you don't have the normal spellbook active, it will become active when you start this battle, and will revert afterwards.
param=param_2102,Raaaa
param=param_2118,vorbis_8348
param=param_2119,vorbis_8348
param=param_2120,vorbis_8348
param=param_2121,vorbis_8348
param=param_2122,4000
param=param_2099,0
param=param_2101,aif_dom_second_dagannoth_mother

// 2762
[struct_2762]
param=param_2095,The Untouchable
param=param_2096,7
param=param_2153,npc_14484
param=param_2168,npc_14485
param=param_2123,37
param=param_2124,31
param=param_2097,1
param=param_2184,A figment of your imagination, this creature thrives on being practically impossible to injure. Its gelatinous quality means it's difficult to deal an impact. And anyone fighting it ends up all slimy.<br><br><col=F5B241>Quest</col>: Dream Mentor<br><br><col=F5B241>Combat</col>: Fights using melee only but takes a fair amount to get in a hit. At least good old Cyrisus is there to help a little.
param=param_2102,Grrrr
param=param_2118,vorbis_9166
param=param_2119,vorbis_9166
param=param_2120,vorbis_9166
param=param_2121,vorbis_9166
param=param_2122,900
param=param_2099,0
param=param_2101,aif_dom_untouchable

// 2763
[struct_2763]
param=param_2095,Damis, Fareed, Kamil and Dessous
param=param_2096,8
param=param_2153,npc_14582
param=param_2154,npc_14584
param=param_2155,npc_14579
param=param_2156,npc_14580
param=param_2168,npc_14587
param=param_2169,npc_14589
param=param_2170,npc_14585
param=param_2171,npc_14586
param=param_2123,38
param=param_2124,33
param=param_2125,37
param=param_2126,32
param=param_2127,37
param=param_2128,31
param=param_2129,38
param=param_2130,30
param=param_2097,2
param=param_2184,These four foes feature as guardians to four diamonds used to gain entrance to a pyramid in the Kharidian desert.<br><br><col=F5B241>Quest</col>: Desert Treasure<br><br><col=F5B241>Combat</col>: You need to fight this dangerous quartet together. Damis has two versions that you must defeat and attacks with melee. Fareed will penalise anyone not wearing ice gloves, attacking with his magic fire attacks. Kamil fights with magic and will occasionally freeze you. Dessous will make use of his patented bat attack to deal magic and ranged damage, should you choose to use one of those protection prayers.
param=param_2102,Attack!
param=param_2103,Don't let it leave this place
param=param_2104,Kill!
param=param_2105,We will destroy you
param=param_2118,vorbis_8633
param=param_2119,vorbis_8633
param=param_2120,vorbis_8633
param=param_2121,vorbis_8633
param=param_2122,7500
param=param_2099,0
param=param_2101,graphic_8244

// 2764
[struct_2764]
param=param_2095,The Everlasting and The Illusive
param=param_2096,9
param=param_2153,npc_14541
param=param_2154,npc_14523
param=param_2168,npc_14542
param=param_2169,npc_14524
param=param_2123,37
param=param_2124,31
param=param_2125,38
param=param_2126,30
param=param_2097,2
param=param_2184,These two creatures are the stuff of (very bizarre) dreams. One of them tries very little to avoid confrontation but is incredibly tough, whereas the other is a nuisance to chase down yet can be killed with a couple of blows.<br><br><col=F5B241>Quest</col>: Dream Mentor<br><br><col=F5B241>Combat</col>: One very tough, one tricky to reach. They both attack with melee, but you'll have Cyrisus with you to help out a bit.
param=param_2102,Roarrrr
param=param_2103,Squeek
